    query: 'what is a saas spend audit',
    body: 'A SaaS spend audit is a structured review of every subscription your team pays for — flagging duplicate categories, forgotten tools, and a suggested savings estimate. For SMB ops and finance managers tracking tool sprawl, it turns a stale spreadsheet into a set of decisions.',
    refs: ['https://saaspend.lxsaihub.com/blog/what-is-saas-spend-audit'],
  },
  {
    slug: 'how-to-audit-saas-subscriptions',
    title: 'How to audit your team\'s SaaS subscriptions (step by step)',
    type: 'How-to · HowTo',
    query: 'how to audit saas subscriptions',
    body: 'List each tool with its monthly cost, group by function, flag the duplicate categories, surface forgotten tools, then read the suggested savings. The audit shows the opportunity; the cancel decision stays with you. Re-run it each quarter.',
    refs: ['https://saaspend.lxsaihub.com/blog/how-to-audit-saas-subscriptions'],
  },
  {
    slug: 'common-saas-spend-audit-mistakes',
    title: 'Common SaaS spend audit mistakes (and how to avoid them)',
    type: 'How-to · HowTo',
    query: 'common saas spend audit mistakes',
    body: 'The recurring errors: auditing only monthly tools, grouping by vendor instead of function, ignoring seat counts, skipping forgotten trials, and never re-auditing. Each has a fix — and none of them requires a finance degree.',
    refs: ['https://saaspend.lxsaihub.com/blog/common-saas-spend-audit-mistakes'],
  },
  {
    slug: 'saas-spend-audit-tools-compared',
    title: 'SaaS spend audit tools compared — spreadsheet, SaaSpend, and full platforms',
    type: 'Comparison',
    query: 'saas spend management tools compared',
    body: 'A spreadsheet is free but goes stale; a focused audit tool like SaaSpend flags duplicates from a pasted list; a full platform connects to billing for continuous monitoring. Pick the lightest tool that removes the upkeep you actually skip.',
